{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "def derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs represent coefficients of a polynomial.\n    xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[2] * x^2 + ....\n     Return derivative of this polynomial in the same form.\n    >>> derivative([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    [1, 4, 12, 20]\n    >>> derivative([1, 2, 3])\n    [2, 6]\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(xs)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return []\n\n    # The derivative of c_0 + c_1*x + c_2*x^2 + ... + c_k*x^k is\n    # c_1 + 2*c_2*x + 3*c_3*x^2 + ... + k*c_k*x^(k-1)\n    # So, the new coefficient for x^j (in the derivative) is (j+1)*c_{j+1} (from original)\n    # where j ranges from 0 to n-2\n    ds = [0] * (n - 1)\n    for k in range(n - 1):\n        ds[k] = (k + 1) * xs[k + 1]\n\n    return ds"}
